@baseUrl = http://127.0.0.1:8000/api

### 1. Is room 1 available? (should be false, John Smith has it)
GET {{baseUrl}}/rooms/1/availability?check_in=2026-11-29&check_out=2026-12-02
Accept: application/json

### 2. Create booking - success (201)
POST {{baseUrl}}/bookings
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "room_id": 2,
  "guest_name": "Jane Doe",
  "guest_email": "jane@example.com",
  "check_in": "2026-12-10",
  "check_out": "2026-12-13"
}

### 3. Create booking - room already taken (409)
POST {{baseUrl}}/bookings
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "room_id": 1,
  "guest_name": "Mark Lee",
  "guest_email": "mark@example.com",
  "check_in": "2026-11-29",
  "check_out": "2026-12-02"
}

### 4. Create booking - validation errors (422)
POST {{baseUrl}}/bookings
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "room_id": 999,
  "guest_email": "not-an-email",
  "check_in": "2026-12-10",
  "check_out": "2026-12-05"
}

### 5. Show booking
GET {{baseUrl}}/bookings/1
Accept: application/json

### 6. Cancel booking
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/bookings/1/cancel
Accept: application/json


### 7. Hotel with prices converted to USD
GET {{baseUrl}}/hotels/1?currency=USD
Accept: application/json